<title>GERMANY: Munich Re denies hidden reserves of 60 bln.</title>
<headline>Munich Re denies hidden reserves of 60 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German reinsurance group Muenchener Rueckversicherungs AG, or Munich Re, on Monday denied a recent analyst's estimate which placed a figure of 60 billion marks on its undisclosed, or &quot;hidden&quot; reserves.</p>
<p>Management board chairman Hans-Juergen Schinzler told a news conference: &quot;That figure is totally off beam. It is really far too high.&quot;</p>
<p>Schinzler added that Munich Re, along with other German insurance companies, would reveal its hidden reserves in 1998.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
